aas (0.3.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * A volume limit, volume_limit_db in the config or limit_db through the
    API: a ceiling applied in software on top of any volume, which no
    player and no bit-perfect mode can get around.
  * clock = "capture": a board whose card only captures, an ADC with no
    DAC, runs its mix on the capture card's clock and plays nowhere
    itself; chosen on its own for such a card.
  * AirPlay outputs: [[airplay]] plays the master mix to one AirPlay
    receiver, as AirPlay 1 or, with protocol = "airplay2", AirPlay 2
    with transient pairing and encrypted audio. It connects on signal
    and disconnects after idle_s of silence, or stays connected with
    connect = "always". latency_ms is 1500 by default, down to 50.

 -- HiFiBerry <info@hifiberry.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 06:02:22 +0000

aas (0.2.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Bluetooth audio under aas: drop-ins for bluez-alsa's bluealsa and
    bluealsa-aplay units run them only when aas is chosen, as the A2DP
    sink, playing into aas with the phone's volume on Master. Under
    PipeWire both are skipped and PipeWire's bluez5 stays the sink.
  * An upgrade no longer stops a running aas without starting it again:
    the device was silent until the next boot. It is restarted instead.

 -- HiFiBerry <info@hifiberry.com>  Tue, 17 Nov 2026 13:51:53 +0000

aas (0.1.0) trixie; urgency=medium

  * First packaged release: the aas audio server and its command-line
    client, and the ALSA plugin as libasound2-plugin-aas.
  * hifiberry-audio-server switches a device between PipeWire and aas.
    The packages are installed disabled and change nothing until it is run.
  * aas-config writes /etc/aas/aas.toml from the HiFiBerry system info at
    every boot; /etc/aas/aas.local.toml is merged over it.

 -- HiFiBerry <info@hifiberry.com>  Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0000
